{"ts": 1791258361.395052, "type": "step", "step": 11, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the key eval idea for the build: compare **pass@k** with **pass^k**. \n\n- **pass@k** = at least one of k tries succeeds.\n- **pass^k** = all k tries succeed.\n\nFor a build writeup, a strong eval usually explains which one matches the deployment goal and why. If the goal is reliability, **pass^k** is the stricter, more deployment-like measure. If the goal is \u201ccan it solve the task at least once if sampled multiple times?\u201d, **pass@k** is more appropriate.\n\nAlso remember the other eval distinction: **proxy vs direct measures**. A proxy is something easier to measure that stands in for the real goal; a direct measure is closer to the actual outcome you care about.\n\nTry this: write 2\u20134 sentences in your eval section answering:\n1) Which metric you used, \n2) why it matches your goal, and \n3) what its limitation is.\n\nIf you want, paste your draft here and I\u2019ll help you tighten it.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.17476759445489312, "pomdp": 0.17476759445489312, "pass_k": 0.37833470247578516}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9326300046159877, "motivation": 0.8147028832022861, "reliance": 0.48500382521680074, "persistence": 0.41823273111755155, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.32174026877242917, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.36461343048320694, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
