{"ts": 1791258382.357449, "type": "step", "step": 34, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Nice \u2014 you\u2019ve got the eval concept. The last thing to do is make the writeup cleaner and less repetitive.\n\nI\u2019d suggest this final structure:\n- **What I built:** one or two sentences describing the environment definition + evaluation write-up.\n- **Environment definition:** keep your state/actions description.\n- **Evaluation:** keep the pass@k vs pass^k explanation, but shorten it a bit and make the goal explicit.\n\nA polished version of the evaluation idea could be:\n\n\u201cI evaluated the build using a metric that matches deployment reliability. pass@k checks whether at least one of k runs succeeds, while pass^k requires all k runs to succeed. Because reliability matters for deployment, pass^k is the stricter metric, though pass@k is still useful for measuring whether the system can succeed at least once.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can help you trim the duplicate sections next.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=38 messages 4m", "t": 42, "activity": [{"t": 38, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.17476759445489312, "pomdp": 0.17476759445489312, "pass_k": 0.7962582271086565}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9026300046159876, "motivation": 0.4147028832022859, "reliance": 0.5050038252168008, "persistence": 0.41823273111755155, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.32174026877242917, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.36461343048320694, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.2674224418999995, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
